# .obsidianignore — release-manifest + graph-hygiene CONVENTION.
# IMPORTANT: Obsidian does NOT read this file. It is not an Obsidian feature
# and does not hide anything from the Obsidian graph view or content indexing.
# It is a convention consumed by bin/release.sh and the docs to mark the
# bundled reference cluster (examples/) as graph-hygiene-excluded content.
# examples/ IS indexed by Dataview by default.
#
# To actually exclude examples/ from your own Obsidian vault, use
# Settings → Files & Links → Excluded files (writes app.json userIgnoreFilters).
# (If you run the Dataview fixtures, do NOT exclude examples/ — they must stay
# indexed for the fixture queries to resolve.)
examples/
